message: "If you use Computer Evolution Lab in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Computer Evolution Lab"
type: software
version: 6.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
abstract: >-
  An interactive, browser-based museum of 49 historical and frontier computers in four
  Circles (personal and hard-wired machines, mainframes and servers, supercomputers, and
  quantum computers), each shown as a 3D scene with an 11-rung abstraction stack from
  physics to software. Many exhibits run working emulators or simulators, including a 6502
  core that passes Klaus Dormann's functional test, an Intel 8080 core that passes the
  classic CP/M CPU diagnostics, a cycle-stepped RV32IM pipeline, a PDP-8, and a Burroughs
  B1700 micro-machine built from its Systems Reference Manual.
